# --- Model weights ---
# The two production checkpoints are TRACKED on purpose: `inference/model_loader.py`
# loads them at request time, so a fresh clone has to contain them or /predict and
# /gradcam answer 503. Both are far below GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit
# (~16 MB CFP, ~48 MB UWF).
#
# Everything else that lands in backend/models/ stays ignored. Note that git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent *directory* is excluded, so the pattern
# below excludes the directory's contents (`backend/models/*`) rather than the
# directory itself, which keeps the two negations effective.
*.onnx
backend/models/*
!backend/models/.gitkeep
!backend/models/EfficientNetB0_CFP_final.pth
!backend/models/EfficientNetB0_UWF_final.pt

# --- Flutter (frontend project not created yet) ---
frontend/.dart_tool/
frontend/.flutter-plugins
frontend/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
frontend/.packages
frontend/build/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/**/android/local.properties
frontend/**/ios/Pods/
frontend/**/macos/Pods/
frontend/pubspec.lock

# --- OS ---
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# --- Uploads / generated reports ---
# Anchored to the repository root. An unanchored "reports/" matches at any depth
# and would silently exclude any source directory that happens to share the
# name, so the leading slash is the fix. Note that git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, which rules out a "!..." negation here.
uploads/
/reports/
